  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).<br />Assertion (A) : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> in water is more stable than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>.<br />Reason (R) : Enthalpy of hydration for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is much less than that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :<br />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4NI3b",
      "text": "&nbsp;Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hxjZe",
      "text": "(A) is correct but (R) is not correct.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zo8Bp",
      "text": "(A) is not correct but (R) is correct.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "87rqS",
      "text": "Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A).",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>Cu</mi></math><br />The stability of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math> rather than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, is due to the much more negative <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>hyd</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math> than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, which more than compensates for the second ionisation enthalpy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).</p>",
